== whoami, unauthenticated
### whoami A no credential
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --server http://127.0.0.1:4291 whoami
    grain: not signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 (it accepts access-code): run grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291
    -> exit=3
### whoami A no credential --json
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --server http://127.0.0.1:4291 -json whoami
    {"error":{"code":"unauthenticated","message":"not signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 (it accepts access-code): run grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291","fix":"grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291"}}
    -> exit=3
== login A with the access code (stdin)
### login A --token-stdin without --auth
$ sh -c /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name a --token-stdin < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain: stdin did not hold a gma_ token; pass --auth access-code to store an access code
    -> exit=2
### login A --token-stdin --auth access-code
$ sh -c /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name a --token-stdin --auth access-code < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain login: warning: the access code grants full operator authority over the deployment; turn on externalAgentApi in Settings and use `grain login --issue-token` for a scoped token
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 as context a (access-code)
    -> exit=0
    -rw------- /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/config.json
    -rw------- /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/a
ok(config.json): secret absent from /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/config.json
### whoami (current=a)
$ /home/debian/bin/grain whoami
    context: a
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4291
    principal: operator
    -> exit=0
== login B: access code in GRAIN_TOKEN, mint a gma_ token
### login B refuses to keep the access code
$ env GRAIN_TOKEN=WQC5-E7F7-OVSJ-4SRL-LPSK-5CTC-WCLH-6NU7 /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4292 --name b
    grain: not storing the token -token gave: http://127.0.0.1:4292 accepts gma_ tokens, so mint one with --issue-token (or pass --auth access-code to keep the access code anyway)
    -> exit=2
### login B --issue-token
$ env GRAIN_TOKEN=WQC5-E7F7-OVSJ-4SRL-LPSK-5CTC-WCLH-6NU7 /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4292 --name b --issue-token --expires 1d
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4292 as context b (external-token)
    -> exit=0
    -rw------- /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/b
    stored credential for b is a gma_ token
ok(config.json): secret absent from /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/config.json
### whoami (current=b, gma_)
$ /home/debian/bin/grain whoami
    context: b
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4292
    principal: agent:external:cli-debuerreotype-b-to5lab
    owner: debian
    scope set: grain/external-dev
    scopes: ci:read, ci:write, deployment:read, merge:write, repos:read, sandboxes:read, tasks:read, tasks:write, templates:read
    expires: 2026-11-08T22:32:35Z
    -> exit=0
### context list
$ /home/debian/bin/grain context list
      a	http://127.0.0.1:4291	access-code
    * b	http://127.0.0.1:4292	external-token
    -> exit=0
### context show
$ /home/debian/bin/grain context show
    name: b
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4292
    auth: external-token
    credential: file:b
    tokenId: 1
    -> exit=0
== precedence: --server > GRAIN_SERVER > --context/GRAIN_CONTEXT > current
### context use a
$ /home/debian/bin/grain context use a
    using context a (http://127.0.0.1:4291)
    -> exit=0
### whoami --context b (flag beats current)
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --context b whoami
    context: b
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4292
    principal: agent:external:cli-debuerreotype-b-to5lab
    owner: debian
    scope set: grain/external-dev
    scopes: ci:read, ci:write, deployment:read, merge:write, repos:read, sandboxes:read, tasks:read, tasks:write, templates:read
    expires: 2026-11-08T22:32:35Z
    -> exit=0
### GRAIN_CONTEXT=b whoami
$ env GRAIN_CONTEXT=b /home/debian/bin/grain whoami
    context: b
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4292
    principal: agent:external:cli-debuerreotype-b-to5lab
    owner: debian
    scope set: grain/external-dev
    scopes: ci:read, ci:write, deployment:read, merge:write, repos:read, sandboxes:read, tasks:read, tasks:write, templates:read
    expires: 2026-11-08T22:32:35Z
    -> exit=0
### GRAIN_CONTEXT=b --context a whoami (flag beats env)
$ env GRAIN_CONTEXT=b /home/debian/bin/grain --context a whoami
    context: a
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4291
    principal: operator
    -> exit=0
### GRAIN_SERVER=B with current=a: a's access code must not travel to B
$ env GRAIN_SERVER=http://127.0.0.1:4292 /home/debian/bin/grain whoami
    grain: not signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4292 (it accepts access-code, external-token): run grain login http://127.0.0.1:4292
    -> exit=3
### --server A with --context b: b's gma_ must not travel to A
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --context b --server http://127.0.0.1:4291 whoami
    grain: not signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 (it accepts access-code): run grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291
    -> exit=3
### GRAIN_TOKEN overrides the context credential (garbage token)
$ env GRAIN_TOKEN=gma_not_a_real_token /home/debian/bin/grain --context b whoami
    grain: the grain daemon at http://127.0.0.1:4292 (from context b) refused this CLI's credentials (grain server: invalid external agent bearer token (401 Unauthorized)): the token from $GRAIN_TOKEN was refused
    -> exit=3
### GRAIN_TOKEN=<A code> with --server A, no context
$ env GRAIN_TOKEN=BEFD-5JHV-6FP4-34MX-SQ3Z-QJAF-LJMF-7LP4 /home/debian/bin/grain --server http://127.0.0.1:4291 whoami
    context: a
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4291
    principal: operator
    -> exit=0
### --context nope
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --context nope whoami
    grain: no context named "nope" (from -context) in the grain config: `grain context list` shows the ones there are
    -> exit=2
== insecure credential file is refused
### whoami --context a with 0644 credential
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --context a whoami
    grain: refusing to read /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/a: its mode is 0644, so other accounts can read it; run chmod 0600 /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/a
    -> exit=3
== argv: a long-running command's /proc/<pid>/cmdline holds no secret
ok(ps): gma_ token absent from ps auxww
== keyring: DBUS set, secret-tool absent -> 0600 file
### login A (no secret-tool on PATH)
$ sh -c PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name a2 --token-stdin --auth access-code < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain login: warning: the access code grants full operator authority over the deployment; turn on externalAgentApi in Settings and use `grain login --issue-token` for a scoped token
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 as context a2 (access-code)
    -> exit=0
== keyring: a fake secret-tool that records its argv (stdin is the secret)
### login A into the keyring
$ sh -c PATH=/tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/fakebin:$PATH /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name k --token-stdin --auth access-code < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain login: warning: the access code grants full operator authority over the deployment; turn on externalAgentApi in Settings and use `grain login --issue-token` for a scoped token
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 as context k (access-code)
    -> exit=0
    secret-tool argv: store --label=grain/k service grain account k
ok(secret-tool-argv): secret absent from /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/fakekeyring/argv.log
    credentials dir: a
    credentials dir: a2
    credentials dir: b
### whoami --context k (keyring reachable)
$ env PATH=/tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/fakebin:/usr/bin:/bin /home/debian/bin/grain --context k whoami
    context: k
    server: http://127.0.0.1:4291
    principal: operator
    -> exit=0
### whoami --context k (keyring unreachable: no DBUS)
$ env -u DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS /home/debian/bin/grain --context k whoami
    grain: the credential for context k is in the OS keyring, which this session cannot reach
    -> exit=3
== keyring locked -> falls back to the 0600 file
### login A with a locked keyring
$ sh -c PATH=/tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/fakebin:$PATH FAKE_KEYRING_LOCKED=1 /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name locked --token-stdin --auth access-code < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain login: warning: the access code grants full operator authority over the deployment; turn on externalAgentApi in Settings and use `grain login --issue-token` for a scoped token
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 as context locked (access-code)
    -> exit=0
    -rw------- /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/locked
== file -> keyring re-login leaves no stale file
### login A as file context fk
$ sh -c PATH=/usr/bin:/bin /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name fk --token-stdin --auth access-code < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain login: warning: the access code grants full operator authority over the deployment; turn on externalAgentApi in Settings and use `grain login --issue-token` for a scoped token
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 as context fk (access-code)
    -> exit=0
### re-login fk with the keyring reachable
$ sh -c PATH=/tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/fakebin:$PATH /home/debian/bin/grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291 --name fk --token-stdin --auth access-code < /tmp/w/srv-a/code
    grain login: warning: the access code grants full operator authority over the deployment; turn on externalAgentApi in Settings and use `grain login --issue-token` for a scoped token
    signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 as context fk (access-code)
    -> exit=0
STALE: /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/fk still holds the old secret
== logout scrubs
### logout k while the keyring is unreachable
$ env -u DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS /home/debian/bin/grain logout k
    signed out of context k
    -> exit=0
STALE: keyring still holds k's secret after logout
### logout b (revokes the gma_ token)
$ /home/debian/bin/grain logout b
    signed out of context b
    -> exit=0
ok: credentials/b removed
### the revoked gma_ token no longer signs in
$ env GRAIN_TOKEN=gma_70034128dd589a45bd4a85b57e043ecd /home/debian/bin/grain --server http://127.0.0.1:4292 whoami
    grain: the grain daemon at http://127.0.0.1:4292 refused this CLI's credentials (grain server: external agent bearer token has been revoked (401 Unauthorized)): the token from $GRAIN_TOKEN was refused
    -> exit=3
### logout a
$ /home/debian/bin/grain logout a
    signed out of context a
    -> exit=0
### whoami --context a after logout
$ /home/debian/bin/grain --context a whoami
    grain: not signed in to http://127.0.0.1:4291 (it accepts access-code): run grain login http://127.0.0.1:4291
    -> exit=3
    still holds A code: /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/fk
    still holds A code: /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/locked
    still holds A code: /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/a2
    600 /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/config.json
    600 /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/fk
    600 /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/locked
    600 /tmp/grain-ctx.r0dwFy/.config/grain/credentials/a2
